"""The allow-list of the hot-code placement check (CPU audit K6; tools/hot_reach.py, run by tools/build.py).

A function that the audio path reaches (see tools/hot_reach.py for how) must sit in on-chip RAM (hot block, range X or Z). One that sits in the
XIP flash instead must be named here with a one-line reason, or the build fails. Two honest reasons: it runs once per event (a note-on, a
load, a mode change), not per sample or block; or it runs per block but moving it costs range Z that is not there (say how many bytes, and
what was measured).

Seeded on 2026-11-08 from the build of fix/b3-k6 (DUELL_TIDE=1, DUELL_RAMPLACE=1) without moving any function: every entry is a function that was
in the flash at that moment. The "K6 baseline" entries are NOT a judgement that the flash is right for them. The mix and effect stage entries (and the FM6 / morph / twocore helpers added after) were reviewed on 12 November 2026 (b10 round 5; docs/audits/2026-11-08/flash-hot/REVIEW_2026-11-12.md): each reason says per block, per sample when on, or event, and either "RAM candidate" or why it stays in the flash.
When you move a function to range Z, delete its line (the build then says so). Do not add a line to get a build through without a real reason.
"""
